ntime/test_plan26_topology.py -q` | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_real.txt` (**38 passed** — real, unpatched, no plugin, no schema modification) |\n207\t| `python3 -m pytest -q` (ambient) | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/ambient_pytest.txt` (746 passed, 4 skipped, 282 subtests passed) |\n208\t| `python3 -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q -rs` (ambient) | 0 | 1 skipped: \"plan26 hash-locked environment not installed ... No module named 'langgraph'\" — the intended module-level skip, same pattern as N10/N21 |\n209\t\n210\tGeneration 6 (B-4 rework), run in the hash-locked environment N30 built and left\n211\tinstalled (`/tmp/plan26_n30_verify`, same `requirements/plan26.lock`):\n212\t\n213\t| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n214\t|---|---:|---|\n215\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q` | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen6.txt` (**38 passed** against the now fully-wired unit path) |\n216\t| negative probes: each re-scoped assertion violated on purpose | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/negative_probes_gen6.txt` (all three fail as required — none of the re-scoped assertions passes vacuously) |\n217\t| `python3 -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q -rs` (ambient) | 0 | 1 skipped, the same intended module-level skip |\n218\t\n219\tThe negative probes exist because \"assert the property against a bigger graph\"\n220\tis exactly the kind of re-scope that can quietly become a tautology. Removing\n221\t`D06B` from `FANOUT_GUARDS` leaves the discovery superstep unbounded and the\n222\tcycle test fails; naming a non-barrier as `M04`'s return, or dropping a\n223\tregistered fan-out from the shape table, each fails the fan-out test.\n224\t\n225\tAt the time of this run, sibling rework for N30's B-1/B-2/B-3 was still landing,\n226\tso `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` and\n227\t`test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py` were red in the same environment. None of\n228\tthose rows is `test_plan26_topology.py`, and none is in this node's write set.\n229\t\n230\t### Generation 7 (B-6/B-9 rework)\n231\t\n232\tRun in `/tmp/plan26_n20_verify`, the environment this node built at generation 4\n233\tfrom `requirements/plan26.lock` with `pip install --require-hashes`\n234\t(`venv_install.txt`), still holding `langgraph 1.2.9`.\n235\t\n236\t| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n237\t|---|---:|---|\n238\t| `/tmp/plan26_n20_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q` | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen7.txt` (**39 passed**; the baseline before this rework was 37 passed / 2 failed, exactly B-9's two rows) |\n239\t| one real episode of the real compiled graph, no pytest and no in-memory patch in the path | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/d90_dispatch_trace_gen7.txt` |\n240\t| negative probes: each generation-7 assertion violated on purpose | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/negative_probes_gen7.txt` (all four reject) |\n241\t| `python3 -m pytest -q -rs` (ambient) | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/ambient_pytest_gen7.txt` (**806 passed, 12 skipped, 0 failed**, 282 subtests passed; every skip is a \"langgraph absent from the ambient interpreter\" module skip plus N10's `pip-tools` skip) |\n242\t\n243\t#### B-6 verified on the real graph\n244\t\n245\tThe point of B-6 is that it was invisible to every test that did not dispatch\n246\tthrough a compiled edge, so the acceptance evidence is a real episode, not an\n247\tassertion. Streamed from the real `build_curriculum_factory_graph`, with\n248\t`routing.py` exactly as it sits on disk and nothing patched in memory:\n249\t\n250\t```text\n251\tD00 -> D01 -> D02 -> D03 -> D04 -> D05\n252\tD06_COMPILE_SOURCE_REQUESTS      guard=discovery_fanout\n253\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT        guard=authorized        <- 2 reservations committed\n254\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES        (Send worker 1 of 2)\n255\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES        (Send worker 2 of 2)\n256\tD06B_RETRIEVE_SOURCE_CANDIDATES  guard=interpretation_fanout\n257\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT        guard=authorized        <- 2 more\n258\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES        (Send worker 1 of 2)\n259\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES        (Send worker 2 of 2)\n260\tD07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES  exact join reached and passed\n261\tD98_WRITE_TERMINAL\n262\t```\n263\t\n264\tThis is the trace N30 verified for the recipe in memory\n265\t(`evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/blocker_probe_d90_recipe.txt`), now produced by\n266\tcommitted code. Before this rework the same episode reached M01 unreserved and\n267\twas classified `system` by D91 at the first dispatch. D07 still ends on a\n268\t`schema_contract` system failure — the synthetic fixture engine root has no\n269\t`schemas/manifest_domain.metaschema.v1.json` — which is the identical stopping\n270\tpoint N30's probe recorded and is a fixture limit, not a routing one.\n271\t\n272\tFour reservations were minted for four dispatches, one per fan-out member, which\n273\tis what spec 6.2's \"committed before dispatch\" requires and what every N23\n274\tadapter enforces from the other side.\n275\t\n276\t#### Non-vacuity\n277\t\n278\tThe generation-7 assertions were each violated on purpose and each rejected:\n279\t\n280\t| Violation | Rejected by |\n281\t|---|---|\n282\t| a model fan-out row dispatches straight to its worker | `test_no_compiled_edge_enters_a_model_node_except_from_d90` (M01 gains D06 as a second predecessor) |\n283\t| `D07.sources_admitted` points straight at M02 | the same test, on the guard-table half |\n284\t| `route_attempt_reservation` resolves one job id instead of the reserved map | `test_a_fanout_guard_emits_one_send_per_staged_worker_projection` |\n285\t| a model worker gains a forward successor that is not a declared barrier | `test_every_registered_fanout_has_the_worker_to_barrier_shape` (so widening its exclusion set to cover D91 did not make it vacuous) |\n286\t\n287\tDirect compilation proof, run outside pytest against the production builder with\n288\tno test harness in the path:\n289\t\n290\t```text\n291\t$ /tmp/plan26_n20_verify/bin/python -c \"... build_curriculum_factory_graph(...)\"\n292\tCOMPILED: CompiledStateGraph plan26_curriculum_factory\n293\tnodes: 30\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\tNo diagnostic plugin, monkeypatch, schema substitution, or skip is involved in\n297\tany verdict in this record.\n298\t\n299\tInstalled in the isolated environment: `langgraph 1.2.9`,\n300\t`langgraph-checkpoint-sqlite 3.1.0`, `langgraph-checkpoint 4.2.0`,\n301\t`jsonschema 4.26.0`, `PyYAML 6.0.3`, `Pillow 12.2.0`, `pytest 9.0.3`.\n302\t\n303\t### Generation 8 (out-of-scope `register_workbook_topology` call, rework)\n304\t\n305\tRun in `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify`, the same hash-locked `requirements/plan26.lock`\n306\tenvironment N30 built (`langgraph 1.2.9` confirmed present).\n307\t\n308\t| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n309\t|---|---:|---|\n310\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q` (before the fix, against `graph.py` as it stood at commit `7fbb202`) | 1 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8_before_fix.txt` (37 passed, 2 failed — both on the extra unreachable D24-D32 nodes) |\n311\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py -q` (after removing the `register_workbook_topology` call) | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8.txt` (**39 passed**) |\n312\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_model_nodes.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py -q` | 0 | `results/evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_sibling_suites_gen8.txt` (597 passed — N30/N31/N32's own tests, which build their own builders directly rather than through `build_curriculum_factory_graph`, are unaffected) |\n313\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` (ambient, full repo) | 1 | 1125 passed, 1 skipped, 399 subtests passed, 4 failed — all four failures are in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` against deleted `results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json` fixtures, outside this node's write set and outside `graph.py`/`routing.py`; not caused by this rework |\n314\t\n315\t## Tests\n316\t\n317\t| # | TEST item | Verdict | Backing assertion |\n318\t|---:|---|---|---|\n319\t| 1 | Exact available catalogue compiles; one START; only real D98 reaches END | **PASS** (generation 7: 30 -> 32 bindings, B-9) | `test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables`, `test_start_has_exactly_one_edge_and_d98_is_the_only_registered_end_edge`, `test_the_skeleton_wires_exactly_the_declared_edges` — all three pass against the real unmodified schema: **32** registered nodes (22 N22 + 8 N23 adapters + N23's two `MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES`, D90 and D91, which N30 registered), `START` has exactly one edge (`D00`), and `D98_WRITE_TERMINAL` is the only source of a *registered* END edge. The expected set is composed from the three real inventories rather than a literal, and `len(bindings) == 32` is asserted exactly, so a dropped or smuggled binding fails either way. |\n320\t| 2 | Missing/placeholder/test-only/duplicate/dangling/unreachable fails by stable ID | **PASS** | 7 tests: `N20-BIND-MISSING`, `N20-BIND-PLACEHOLDER` (x2: foreign module and test-local callable), `N20-BIND-UNCALLABLE`, `N20-BIND-DUPLICATE`, `N20-EDGE-DANGLING`, `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED`, plus `N20-GUARD-UNROUTED` for a declared guard value with no destination. All raise before `add_node`, so this is a builder guard, not a runtime crash. Generation 6: the `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED` case now reads its example node from the live `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` rather than naming `D13_RENDER_UNIT`, which N30 has since wired — the rejection is what is under test, not any one node, and the fixture now follows whatever N31/N32 still owe. |\n321\t| 3 | Every cycle crosses a deterministic counter/exhaustion guard | **PASS** (generation 7: the model supersteps now run through D90) | `test_every_cycle_in_the_compiled_graph_crosses_an_exhaustion_guard` enumerates every simple cycle of the really-compiled graph. Each is required to contain a bounding node — one declaring an exhaustion guard value whose destination leaves the cycle, or a fan-out that refuses to dispatch again without a freshly staged worker projection (`RoutingViolation`, proven by calling the guard) — and to have at least one product exit outside itself, so no cycle is a closed trap. Generation 7 changes the shape of the two model supersteps: `D06B -> M01 -> D06B` is now `D06B -> D90 -> M01 -> D06B` and the visual barrier is `D12 -> D90 -> M04 -> D12`, which is a *stronger* bound, since D90 is the node that commits the attempt counter and declares `exhausted -> D98`. The refusal probe follows the `Send`s to D90's guard, which is where a staged packet is now translated. The frozen guard rows for the cycles N31/N32 have yet to wire are still asserted: D17/D18/D29 `convergence_exhausted -> D98`, D90/D91 `exhausted -> D98`, and the unit loop closing only through `D23 -> D05`. Non-vacuity is evidenced, not assumed (`negative_probes_gen6.txt`, `negative_probes_gen7.txt`). |\n322\t| 4 | Models have no edge to acceptance/routing/reduction/resume/terminal authority | **PASS** | `test_no_model_node_has_an_edge_to_an_authority_node` (compiled-edge half, now against the real compiled graph), `test_a_model_node_holds_no_acceptance_reduction_or_terminal_channel_authority`, `test_routing_never_lets_a_model_result_name_its_own_destination` (AST: no model-result guard reads any channel in `MODEL_NODE_WRITABLE_FIELDS` except presence of `source_discoveries`/`source_interpretations`, and names only code-owned destinations), and `test_a_stored_frontier_may_not_name_a_model_node`. See Findings F-02 for the deliberate reading of \"reduction\". |\n323\t| 5 | Source/visual fan-outs use supported `Send` worker->barrier; mixed joins fail | **PASS** (generation 7: re-scoped for B-6, and a new assertion added) | `test_every_registered_fanout_has_the_worker_to_barrier_shape` checks all four registered fan-outs against the compiled graph. The compiled shape is now `dispatcher -> D90 -> worker -> barrier` for the three model fan-outs (D06/D06B -> M01, D12 -> M04) and `dispatcher -> worker -> barrier` for the deterministic one (D10 -> D11): the dispatching guard is asserted to return D90 rather than a `Send` list, and the `Send`s are then asserted against D90's own guard, one per staged member with the member passed through unchanged. Each worker has a compiled edge to the deterministic barrier that owns the denominator (D06B, D07, D12, D12 respectively — never a model node), and its forward successors, recovery destinations aside, are *exactly* its declared barriers. `D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE` joined `D96`/`D98`/`END` in that exclusion set (B-9): a model worker's failure edge is a recovery edge, not a second barrier — and the probe table above shows the widened exclusion did not make the assertion vacuous. The shape table is still asserted total over `FANOUT_GUARDS`. **New at generation 7:** `test_no_compiled_edge_enters_a_model_node_except_from_d90` asserts B-6's inverse over the whole graph — no `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` row names a model node, and every model node's set of compiled predecessors is exactly `{D90}`. The two guard-level tests were re-pointed at D90, which is now where a staged packet becomes `Send`s: `test_a_fanout_guard_emits_one_send_per_staged_worker_projection` (which also asserts D12's guard returns D90) and `test_a_fanout_guard_refuses_an_unstaged_or_mixed_dispatch`. |\n324\t| 6 | Empty subsets and arbitrary manifest lengths remain legal | **PASS** | Four tests: no unit/lesson identifier or manifest-length constant appears in `graph.py`/`routing.py` (AST + substring); an empty deterministic visual subset routes straight to the barrier; an exhausted manifest routes to coverage proof at any length; and `test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest` confirms against the real compiled graph that the registered node set equals the frozen binding inventory with no per-unit node. |\n325\t| 7 | Identical real bindings yield identical digest; callable/schema/prompt drift changes it | **PASS** | All five digest tests pass against the real schema: two independent builds agree, and a changed callable binding, a changed reducer declaration, and a changed prompt file each change the digest; `test_the_digest_ignores_python_object_identity` pins that it is not keyed on object identity. **Production graph digest at generation 8: `f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f`.** It moved from generation 7's `297f0b5f…` for two reasons: this rework dropped the nine unreachable D24-D32 nodes `register_workbook_topology` was wrongly registering into the production compile point, and the model-node/contract bindings the digest also hashes had already drifted from the B-7 rework landed on N22/N23 since generation 7. Generation 7 had moved from generation 6's `d2679804…` for two reasons that are both the property these tests exist to hold: N30 registered D90/D91 (two nodes, fifteen edges), and this node's B-6 rework re-pointed six guard rows, which changes the topology the digest is keyed on. It had moved from generation 5's `4b1f7242…` when N30 registered the per-unit path. Generation 4's provisional diagnostic value `58ef1bd4...` was computed over a patched schema and remains void. |\n326\t| 8 | Production imports contain no handwritten fallback controller | **PASS** | `test_production_graph_imports_contain_no_fallback_controller`: no import or textual reference to `runtime.curriculum_factory_graph`, `CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `session_bridge`, `test_simulated`, or `fallback_controller`, and none of the five forbidden model-invocation packages. `test_only_one_builder_and_one_compile_call_exist` asserts exactly one `build_*graph*` function and exactly one `.compile(` call in `graph.py`. |\n327\t\n328\tTotals: **39 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors, 0 skipped** in the hash-locked\n329\tenvironment (38 at generation 6; the 39th is\n330\t`test_no_compiled_edge_enters_a_model_node_except_from_d90`). The 38th test,\n331\t`test_the_state_schema_declares_no_langgraph_reserved_channel_name` — the\n332\tassertion that reported the generation-4 blocker — is now green, which is the\n333\tacceptance test for the erratum's rework and is retained as a standing\n334\tregression guard against any future reserved-name collision.\n335\t\n336\t### Real binding inventory (32 callables, all production modules)\n337\t\n338\t| Source | Node IDs |\n339\t|---|---|\n340\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.inputs` (N22) | D00, D00R, D01, D02, D03, D04, D92, D96 |\n341\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.sources` (N22) | D05, D06, D06B, D07, D30 |\n342\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.domain` / `.content` (N22) | D08, D09 |\n343\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.visuals` (N22) | D10, D11, D12 |\n344\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.render` / `.review` (N22) | D13, D14, D15 |\n345\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` (N22) | D98 |\n346\t| `runtime.langgraph_factory.model_nodes` (N23) | M01–M08, D90, D91 |\n347\t\n348\tAbsent by construction, not padded: D16–D29, D31, D32 (N31/N32 own the bodies).\n349\tD90/D91 are no longer absent — F-03 recorded them as owed, N23 exported them as\n350\t`MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES` under N30's Finding B-3, and N30 registered them, which\n351\ttakes the inventory from 30 to 32.\n352\t\n353\t### Topology actually registered\n354\t\n355\t```text\n356\tSTART -> D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\n357\tD00  -[fresh]->            D01 -> D02 -> D03\n358\tD00  -[legal resume]->     D00R -> D03\n359\tD00  -[orphan recovery]->  D96 -> D98 -> END\n360\tD03  -[capabilities]->     D04\n361\tD04  -[fresh]->            D05     (frontier: outgoing edges owned by N30)\n362\tD04  -[resume]->           D92     (frontier: outgoing edges owned by N30)\n363\tevery skeleton branch additionally -> D96 (graceful interrupt) and -> D98 (system failure)\n364\t```\n365\t\n366\tThis is the skeleton this node registers, and it is unchanged at generation 6.\n367\tWhat *has* changed is the graph the tests run against: N30 has since registered\n368\tthe per-unit path into the same builder, so D05, D92, D06, D06B, D07, D08, D09,\n369\tD10, D11, D12, D13, D14, D15, D30 and M01–M05 have left `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` and\n370\tare wired for real. `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` now holds exactly M06\n371\t(`N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`), M07 and M08 (`N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS`), so an\n372\tundeclared unwired node still fails the build. The repair cycle and the whole\n373\tD24–D32 workbook branch remain **not** wired and are not claimed here.\n374\t\n375\t### Guard and authority report\n376\t\n377\t`routing.py` implements the complete spec 8.2 table: 39 named pure guard\n378\tfunctions over a frozen `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` table covering all 34 emitting\n379\tnodes, plus `DYNAMIC_GUARDS` (4 rows whose destination is state-carried and\n380\tvalidated against a model-node exclusion), `FANOUT_GUARDS` (4 `Send` rows), and\n381\t`MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS` (7 rows; M01's two supersteps are resolved by result\n382\tpresence). Ordering is failure-before-interrupt, deliberately: an episode that\n383\tbroke *and* was asked to stop terminates as `SYSTEM_FAILURE`, not `INTERRUPTED`.\n384\tAn undeclared guard value raises `RoutingViolation` rather than resolving to a\n385\tterminal, and `assert_guard_table_total()` runs inside the builder so that\n386\tdisagreement fails compilation instead of waiting for a rare edge.\n387\t\n388\tNo model node is a source of any edge into acceptance (D22), checkpoint\n389\tinitialization/correlation (D04, D23), unit selection (D05), workbook assembly\n390\t(D25), release (D32), resume re-entry (D92), or the terminal writer (D98/END).\n391\t\n392\t## Findings\n393\t\n394\t- **F-01 (RESOLVED at generation 5) — was `state_or_reducer` -> N11_STATE_REDUCERS.**\n395\t  `FactoryState.checkpoint_ns` collided with LangGraph 1.2.9's reserved channel\n396\t  set (`langgraph._internal._constants.RESERVED`), so\n397\t  `StateGraph(FactoryState, ...).compile()` raised\n398\t  `ValueError: Channel name 'checkpoint_ns' is reserved` before any Plan 26 code\n399\t  ran. Resolved by N11 (channel declaration) and N22 (three call sites) under\n400\t  `contracts/erratum_checkpoint_ns_rename.v1.md`: the channel is now\n401\t  `checkpoint_namespace`, value unchanged (`\"\"`).\n402\t  Verified here, not taken on report: (a) the real builder compiles, (b) all 38\n403\t  tests pass unpatched, (c)\n404\t  `test_the_state_schema_declares_no_langgraph_reserved_channel_name` — the\n405\t  acceptance test named in generation 4 — is green, and it computes\n406\t  `set(FACTORY_STATE_FIELDS) & set(RESERVED)` dynamically rather than hardcoding\n407\t  the old name, so it will also catch `checkpoint_id` or `configurable` if a\n408\t  future channel ever takes one.\n409\t  This node's own write set required **no change**: the only textual\n410\t  `checkpoint_ns` in `graph.py` / `routing.py` / `test_plan26_topology.py` is a\n411\t  docstring in that test explaining which names LangGraph reserves, which is\n412\t  still factually correct and is deliberately retained.\n413\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n20/reserved-channel/checkpoint_ns` — closed.\n414\t\n415\t- **F-02 (informational, resolved here) — spec 8.1 vs this prompt's TEST 4.**\n416\t  Spec 8.1 wires `M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT -> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` and\n417\t  `M07 -> D28`, while this node's TEST 4 forbids a model edge to \"reduction\".\n418\t  Resolved in favour of the spec's explicit topology: a review is *evidence for*\n419\t  the code-computed denominator, and spec 8.1's own prohibition list names\n420\t  acceptance, terminal, checkpoint initialization, unit selection, workbook\n421\t  assembly, and release — not reduction. \"Models hold no reduction authority\" is\n422\t  therefore proven where it lives, as a channel-authority property\n423\t  (`test_a_model_node_holds_no_acceptance_reduction_or_terminal_channel_authority`:\n424\t  no model may write `deterministic_checks`, `artifact_heads`,\n425\t  `accepted_unit_receipts`, `cursor`, `resume_frontier`, or any terminal\n426\t  channel), not as edge adjacency. No rework requested.\n427\t  Re-verified at generation 5: unchanged, and TEST 4's compiled-edge half now\n428\t  runs against the really-compiled graph rather than a patched one.\n429\t\n430\t- **F-03 (non-blocking) — `model_node_or_projection` -> N23_MODEL_NODES.**\n431\t  D90 and D91 exist only as helper functions (`reserve_model_attempt(state, *,\n432\t  job_id, correlation_key, activation_id, ...)`,\n433\t  `classify_model_failure(failure, *, attempts_used, ...)`), which are\n434\t  keyword-only and cannot be registered with `add_node`. `routing.py` declares\n435\t  their guard rows (`D90.exhausted`, `D91.retry/repair/system/exhausted`) so the\n436\t  destinations are frozen, but N30 cannot wire the repair cycle until N23 (or\n437\t  N30 by agreement) exposes `(state, context)` node callables for them.\n438\t  Not blocking N20: the skeleton wires neither node.\n439\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n20/d90-d91-not-registrable`.\n440\t  Re-verified at generation 5 against N23's current `model_nodes.py` (hash\n441\t  unchanged, `4cfa7de2...`): both signatures are still keyword-only after the\n442\t  first positional parameter (`model_nodes.py:692`, `model_nodes.py:759`), so\n443\t  the finding stands unmodified and is still owed to N23 or N30.\n444\t\n445\t- **F-04 (non-blocking) — `deterministic_node` -> N22_DETERMINISTIC_NODES.**\n446\t  D06, D06B and D10 declare fan-out guards but their catalogue rows do not\n447\t  authorize `pending_packet`, so they stage no worker projections, while D12\n448\t  does (`{\"dispatch\": ..., \"briefs\": [...]}`). `routing.py`'s fan-out guards\n449\t  translate staged material one-for-one and raise `RoutingViolation` when it is\n450\t  absent, rather than materializing a projection at routing time that no\n451\t  denominator committed to (spec section 10). Before N30 can register the source\n452\t  and deterministic-visual `Send` edges, D06/D06B/D10 must stage their packets\n453\t  and have `pending_packet` added to their authorized outputs.\n454\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n20/fanout-packet-not-staged`.\n455\t  Re-verified at generation 5 against N22's generation-4 catalogue: reading\n456\t  `NODE_CATALOGUE[...].outputs` directly still gives `pending_packet` present\n457\t  for `D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN` only, and absent for\n458\t  `D06_COMPILE_SOURCE_REQUESTS`, `D06B_RETRIEVE_SOURCE_CANDIDATES`, and\n459\t  `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS`. The `checkpoint_namespace` rework touched only\n460\t  D04's row and did not disturb this, so the finding stands unmodified.\n461\t\n462\t- **F-05 (informational) — LangGraph does not enforce reachability.**\n463\t  Verified empirically against 1.2.9: an unreachable node and a dead-end node\n464\t  both compile without error; only a conditional-edge target that names an\n465\t  unregistered node is rejected. The builder's own `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED` and\n466\t  `N20-EDGE-DANGLING` checks therefore carry that guarantee, and\n467\t  `compiled.get_graph()` draws a dead-end node as reaching `__end__` — which is\n468\t  why TEST 1 asserts the single *registered* END edge and then requires every\n469\t  other node drawn to `__end__` to be a declared N30 frontier.\n470\t  Still true at generation 5, and now load-bearing rather than hypothetical:\n471\t  TEST 1 makes that distinction on the real compiled graph's 30 nodes.\n472\t\n473\t- **F-06 (informational) — LangGraph injects `Runtime`, not services.**\n474\t  Verified empirically: a node whose second parameter is unannotated receives\n475\t  its default (`None`), so N22's and N23's bodies would have run with\n476\t  `runtime_context=None` had `graph.py` registered them directly. The common\n477\t  node boundary in `graph.py` is what injects `RuntimeContext` from\n478\t  `Runtime.context`, marks a graceful interrupt observed at the atomic boundary,\n479\t  and classifies an unexpected exception as `pending_failure`\n480\t  (`class=system`, `cause=unhandled`) while re-raising LangGraph's own\n481\t  `GraphBubbleUp` control flow untouched.\n482\t  Still true at generation 5: the four boundary tests\n483\t  (`..._injects_the_runtime_context_langgraph_would_not`,\n484\t  `..._classifies_an_unexpected_exception_as_a_system_failure`,\n485\t  `..._graceful_signal_..._routes_through_the_interrupt_gate`,\n486\t  `..._a_classified_failure_outranks_a_graceful_interrupt`) all pass unpatched.\n487\t\n488\t- **F-07 (RESOLVED at generation 6) — N30's B-4, `topology_or_guard`, caused by this node.**\n489\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n30/n20-skeleton-scoped-tests-superseded`. Three tests in\n490\t  this node's write set asserted properties of a skeleton with no unit path:\n491\t  a `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` fixture pinned to `D13_RENDER_UNIT`, \"the compiled graph\n492\t  contains no cycle\", and \"no `Send` fan-out is registered\". N30 wiring spec\n493\t  8.1's per-unit path made all three false without breaking anything — the\n494\t  additive registration is exactly what `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` assigns\n495\t  to N30. Resolved by re-scoping the three assertions onto the compiled graph as\n496\t  it now stands (table at the head of this record) and adding negative probes so\n497\t  the wider assertions cannot pass vacuously. No production code changed; the\n498\t  properties under test are the same ones, held against a larger topology.\n499\t  The lesson worth carrying: an assertion phrased as \"X is absent\" is a\n500\t  statement about the *current* frontier, and a successor doing its job will\n501\t  falsify it. Phrase the invariant instead — \"every X has shape S\" — which is\n502\t  what these three now do.\n503\t\n504\t- **F-08 (RESOLVED at generation 7) — N30's B-6, `topology_or_guard`, this node's defect.**\n505\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n30/model-dispatch-bypasses-d90`. Diagnosed and fixed as\n506\t  described at the head of this record. Two things are worth carrying forward.\n507\t  First, on why it survived four generations of green tests: every predecessor\n508\t  proved its own half by *calling* D90 or the adapters directly, and this node\n509\t  proved the guard table was total and well-typed. Totality is not reachability\n510\t  — a table can name a destination for every guard value and still have no edge\n511\t  that reaches the node that authorizes the dispatch. The generation-7\n512\t  regression is phrased over compiled predecessors precisely so it cannot be\n513\t  satisfied by a table that merely mentions D90.\n514\t  Second, on scope: N30 named three unit-path rows; a fourth (D27 -> M07) had the\n515\t  same defect on the not-yet-wired workbook path and was found by writing the\n516\t  assertion as a total property of `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` rather than as three\n517\t  fixes. A defect report is bounded by what the reporter can execute, and the\n518\t  owner of the table is the one who has to close it everywhere.\n519\t\n520\t- **F-09 (RESOLVED at generation 7) — N30's B-9, `topology_or_guard`, caused by N30.**\n521\t  Fingerprint `plan26/n30/n20-tests-superseded-by-d90-d91-registration`. N30\n522\t  registering D90/D91 made two of this node's assertions false by design, the\n523\t  same pattern as F-07. Applying B-6 in the same generation superseded three\n524\t  more. All five are re-scoped; none is weakened, and the probe table under\n525\t  Commands shows none became vacuous.\n526\t\n527\t### Re-scoped at generation 7\n528\t\n529\t| Test | Was | Now |\n530\t|---|---|---|\n531\t| `test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables` | `set(bindings) == set(registry) \\| set(MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS)`, 30 bindings | also unions `MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES` and asserts 32, with that set's membership (D90, D91) asserted rather than assumed |\n532\t| `test_every_registered_fanout_has_the_worker_to_barrier_shape` | dispatcher's compiled successor is the worker, and the dispatcher's guard emits the `Send`s | dispatcher's successor is D90 for a model fan-out (D11 for the deterministic one), the `Send`s are asserted against D90's guard, and D91 joins the worker-successor exclusion set as a recovery edge (B-9) |\n533\t| `test_every_cycle_in_the_compiled_graph_crosses_an_exhaustion_guard` | the discovery superstep cycle is `{D06B, M01}`, and the dispatcher's guard is probed for the no-staged-packet refusal | the cycle is `{D06B, D90, M01}`, and the refusal is probed at whichever guard now emits the `Send`s |\n534\t| `test_a_fanout_guard_emits_one_send_per_staged_worker_projection` | `route_visual_barrier` returns two `Send`s | `route_visual_barrier` returns D90, and `route_attempt_reservation` returns the two `Send`s |\n535\t| `test_a_fanout_guard_refuses_an_unstaged_or_mixed_dispatch` | the three malformed-packet rejections are asserted on D12's guard | asserted on D90's guard, which is where a staged packet is now translated |\n536\t\n537\t## Invalidated descendants\n538\t\n539\tNone. This node has never modified a predecessor's artifact. Generation 7 edits\n540\t`routing.py` and `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`, both in this node's own\n541\twrite set, and `routing.py`'s change is the rework N30 asked for.\n542\t\n543\tIt does, however, supersede six assertions in **N30's own**\n544\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, which N30 must re-scope — the mirror\n545\timage of B-9, and expected, since two of them are the `test_blocked_*` rows N30\n546\twrote to *record* B-6 and which must now invert:\n547\t\n548\t| N30 test | Why it is now false |\n549\t|---|---|\n550\t| `test_blocked_no_registered_edge_routes_a_model_dispatch_through_d90` | an edge does now route through D90; this is B-6's inversion |\n551\t| `test_blocked_d90s_authorized_guard_cannot_express_a_map` | `route_attempt_reservation` now returns an N-element `Send` list |\n552\t| `test_a_visual_fanout_dispatches_one_send_per_staged_denominator_member` | D12's guard returns D90, so the `Send`s are D90's |\n553\t| `test_a_source_fanout_stages_one_m01_packet_per_request_key` | same, for D06 |\n554\t| `test_a_fanout_with_no_staged_packet_refuses_to_improvise_one` | the refusal moved to D90's guard |\n555\t| `test_the_source_map_reduce_supersteps_execute_as_real_send_fanouts` | asserts the episode ends `SYSTEM_FAILURE` via D91 on an unreserved dispatch; it now reaches D07 |\n556\t\n557\tA seventh row in the same file,\n558\t`test_blocked_a_model_candidate_record_is_not_an_admissible_artifact_version`, is\n559\tred for an unrelated reason — it is B-7's inversion, and N22/N23's B-7 rework has\n560\tsince landed. Not caused by this node and not this node's to re-scope.\n561\t\n562\t## Hashes\n563\t\n564\t| Artifact | SHA-256 |\n565\t|---|---|\n566\t| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | eae00c21bfe55ce6e2d6c4374611db4d84d286218d498fa520e799288e152e26 (was `6361e12c…` at generation 7; generation 8 removes the out-of-scope `register_workbook_topology(builder)` call from `build_curriculum_factory_graph` and corrects two docstrings that referenced it) |\n567\t| `runtime/langgraph_factory/routing.py` | 6be93bf8bd951ae9984f74dc9dbe91c709a41edca0a1a6ff6d72be52cd998079 (was `efcc6db1…`; the B-6 rework, and the first change to this file since generation 4) |\n568\t| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` | 87bd5dc6b3e4da4c6ae4c2646027c648167bf72f9432033c9567c65c752af332 (was `84488301…`; the B-9 re-scopes plus the new B-6 regression) |\n569\t| `implementation.graph.v3.yaml` | ca4835f71750f93880a965a9879e508641b5f9360b82cb5cc8bdec8d57564f30 (was `implementation.graph.v2.yaml` at `96e1948f…` through generation 7) 