 b99e69c541db99e428b0f5f1c3ddfb62c533ad116a16515e553040fb5268a3ad |\n| `results/N30_UNIT_GRAPH.result.v1.md` | ed79b4e2c68621519f7d85b33bd5c19b14f20e1dc7f0e029bd0bf9bc7a08ab35 (as read at generation 7; N30's own file, out of this node's write set, has since changed on disk) |\n| `evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8_before_fix.txt` | a6a3cc2617345e604d66e0bef36c79c4388e786bbd9b2acd58f6b34fdeea40a3 |\n| `evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8.txt` | d793cc1166095a41510890444ae1d4a0c8fe4c85391016ca5167a521800225eb |\n| `evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_sibling_suites_gen8.txt` | 65e7a7fa4d4611aee1d4b52e3633958ce58980ce05cd8e4e631df4bd679b8026 |\n\nGeneration 4's `diag_plugin.py`, `venv_topology_diagnostic.txt`, and\n`diagnostic_topology.txt` were deleted, not merely de-listed: no verdict in\nthis record depends on them, and leaving a schema-patching plugin in an\nevidence directory invites a later node to mistake it for a supported harness.\n\nProduction graph digest at generation 8 (over the real compiled graph,\nreproducible): `f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f`.\nGeneration 7 was `297f0b5f1113aceb902d1793ab1669520c4cdc5575ca5e51c79c3d652c1f5fe3`,\ngeneration 6 `d26798042b0499425055fa4eb995deb2071c00f07f520d4be1fcd3f85429125c`,\nand generation 5 `4b1f7242be5b2f40ac789b38f154ca32d05ef91bd01bdb3745d93ba027fb7361`;\neach move is a real topology or binding change, which is what the digest is\nkeyed on. The generation-8 delta is two-fold: this rework drops the nine\nunreachable D24-D32 nodes that `register_workbook_topology` was wrongly adding\nto the compiled graph, and the model-node/contract bindings the digest also\nhashes had already drifted since generation 7 from the B-7 rework landed on\nN22/N23 (see \"Invalidated descendants\").\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":10,"newStart":1,"newLines":85,"lines":[" # N20_GRAPH_COMPILER result"," "," status: PASSED","-graph_digest: ca4835f71750f93880a965a9879e508641b5f9360b82cb5cc8bdec8d57564f30","+graph_digest: f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f"," node_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N20_graph_compiler.prompt.v2.md (577a251c85b80d00fc0ae3929dc620a5c1b28b79ab970729a0b9428744f4f469)","-generation: 8","+generation: 9","+patch: P-N20-001 (active_patch_ids=[\"P-N20-001\"], patch_chain_sha256=ac6db487d79bdc554dbd58ecbc830e80824344e61ad9b8250711560fae5a966f)"," ","+## Generation-9 rework — P-N20-001 (root cause: N90 finding F1, via P-N31-001)","+","+**Root cause chain.** N90's audit found finding F1: before any real repair/","+acceptance wiring existed, a real episode could never reach `UNIT_ACCEPTED`.","+N31's approved rework `P-N31-001` closes that gap by wiring D16-D23/M06 into","+the one production compiled graph (`build_curriculum_factory_graph` in","+`graph.py`), additively, over and above this node's frozen 32-entry","+`binding_inventory()` — which N31 correctly leaves unchanged, since other","+tests (this node's own, among them) depend on that exact 32-entry contract.","+That correction necessarily makes the compiled graph's node set *wider* than","+`binding_inventory()` from then on: D16-D23 were always excluded from that","+function by design (its own docstring says so), not by oversight.","+","+Three assertions in this node's own `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`","+hardcoded the narrower, pre-correction invariant \"the compiled node set is","+*exactly* `binding_inventory()`\", which is a structural consequence of","+nothing downstream having wired anything yet — not a defect in this node's","+own topology-validation logic (`register_skeleton`, `validate_bindings`,","+`_validate_topology`, `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`), none of which P-N31-001 touches.","+Per this approved immutable patch overlay, the fix is a test-fixture","+correction only, confined to the one file already in this node's write set.","+**Important ordering note, confirmed empirically below:** at the time this","+generation runs, `graph.py` in this repository still only compiles the","+narrow, pre-correction `binding_inventory()` (verified: `graph.py` and","+`routing.py` hashes are byte-identical to generation 8, unchanged by this","+rework) — N31's D16-D23 wiring lands in a separate, isolated attempt and is","+rebased in afterward. The three failures the patch describes therefore do","+not reproduce in this workspace; the fix is verified as correct by","+construction instead (below), exactly as the patch instructs.","+","+**What changed**, all in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`:","+","+| Test | Was (generation 8) | Now (generation 9, P-N20-001) |","+|---|---|---|","+| `test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables` | `set(drawn.nodes) - {START, END} == set(bindings)` (exact equality) | `skeleton_required <= compiled_nodes`, where `skeleton_required = set(G._skeleton_required_nodes()) \\| set(bindings)` — a subset assertion that holds whether the compiled set is today's narrow 32 or a later, legitimately wider one. The existing per-binding production-module loop is retained unchanged, re-deriving `validate_bindings`'s own guarantee for every binding this node owns. |","+| `test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest` | `drawn == set(G.binding_inventory())` (exact equality) | Same subset assertion (`skeleton_required <= drawn`), plus the existing unit/lesson-numbering check unchanged. |","+| `test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` | picked `sorted(G.DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY)[0]` unconditionally as the pop-victim | now filters `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` to keys with **no compiled edge at all** (`set(G.DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY) - wired_endpoints`, computed from the real `compiled` fixture's edge set) before picking one, and asserts at least one such candidate exists. A `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` entry whose node a downstream node has since wired for real — even if the entry itself is left stale in the table — no longer produces a false victim that fails to reproduce `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED`; simulated and confirmed below (`deferred_victim_simulation_gen9.txt`). This is a strictly *stronger* fixture than the patch's literal minimum ask (\"was it wired\") — it defends against a stale-entry edge case the patch's own narrative did not need to name because it was describing D16's future removal from the table, not a leftover key. |","+","+None of `register_skeleton`, `validate_bindings`, `_validate_topology`,","+`DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`, `routing.py`'s guard tables, N31's `repair.py`/","+`acceptance.py`, or D16-D23's registration logic were touched, per the","+patch's explicit instruction. `graph.py` and `routing.py` are byte-identical","+to generation 8.","+","+**Verification.** Because the widening this patch anticipates has not","+happened in this workspace yet, correctness is shown two ways rather than by","+reproducing a failure that cannot occur here:","+","+1. All 39 tests in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` still pass","+   unmodified against today's narrow, unwidened graph","+   (`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen9.txt`, **39 passed**), and","+   the full N10/N11/N22/N23 verification command stays green across all four","+   of its test files (`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_sibling_suites_gen9.txt`,","+   **543 passed, 187 subtests passed**, covering","+   `test_plan26_topology.py`/`test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py`/","+   `test_plan26_model_nodes.py`/`test_plan26_state_reducers.py`).","+2. Two standalone simulations construct the exact future scenario the patch","+   describes — a hand-widened compiled graph with an extra node/edge beyond","+   `binding_inventory()` (`widening_simulation_gen9.py`/`.txt`), and a","+   `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` entry whose node has been wired for real but is left","+   stale in the table (`deferred_victim_simulation_gen9.py`/`.txt`) — and","+   prove, outside pytest, against the real compiled graph: (a) the new","+   subset assertion